# K03 S6 control (Codex K03-CALLABLE-PATH-20261007-25): a path whose last field is a number is read, never called --
# beside a callable field in the same Structure; nothing runs, Holder's own statement `bump()` neither.  v is 5, w 6:
# exit 7; 81 if anything ran, 83 a wrong value.
int: hits 0
int: seen 0
fn: tick () int
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
    return: node\hits
end: tick
fn: bump () int
    node\seen: node\seen + 1
    return: 0
end: bump
fn: count () int
    return: node\hits
end: count
fn: saw () int
    return: node\seen
end: saw
Holder:
    fn: tick
    int: tag 5
    bump()
end: Holder
fn: run () int
    int: v Holder\tag
    int: w Holder\tag + 1
    if: saw() != 0 || count() != 0
        return: 81
    if: v + w != 11
        return: 83
    return: 7
end: run
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: run(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
